! IEEE-13 configuration 601 overhead line, defined through OpenDSS WireData +
! LineGeometry so OpenDSS computes the series/shunt matrices from first
! principles. This is the reference for the geometry cross-check in
! test/lineconstants_tests.jl: BMOPFTools builds the SAME geometry by hand as
! wire_data/line_geometry and its compile_linecode output is compared against
! the matrices OpenDSS returns here.
!
! Notes:
!  - reduce=no keeps the full 4x4 (a,b,c,n) primitive matrix, matching what
!    BMOPFTools compiles (it never Kron-reduces circuit conductors).
!  - EarthModel=Carson is OpenDSS's constant-term truncation == BMOPFTools
!    "modified_carson". (OpenDSS DEFAULTS to Deri; the test also drives a Deri
!    variant by editing this line in-memory.)
!  - Line units=m so Lines.RMatrix()/XMatrix() come back in ohm/m and
!    Lines.CMatrix() in nF/m, directly comparable to BMOPFTools per-metre codes.
!  - Conductor data are the published Kersting 556,500 26/7 ACSR (phases) and
!    4/0 6/1 ACSR (neutral), on the 500-series pole-top spacing.

clear
new circuit.ieee13_601 basekv=4.16 phases=3 bus1=sourcebus
set defaultbasefreq=60
set earthmodel=Carson

new wiredata.acsr556 rac=0.1859 gmr=0.0313 radius=0.4635 runits=mi gmrunits=ft radunits=in normamps=730
new wiredata.acsr40  rac=0.592  gmr=0.00814 radius=0.2815 runits=mi gmrunits=ft radunits=in normamps=340

new linegeometry.g601 nconds=4 nphases=3 reduce=no
~ cond=1 wire=acsr556 x=2.5 h=29 units=ft
~ cond=2 wire=acsr556 x=0   h=29 units=ft
~ cond=3 wire=acsr556 x=7.0 h=29 units=ft
~ cond=4 wire=acsr40  x=4.0 h=25 units=ft

new line.l1 bus1=sourcebus bus2=b2 geometry=g601 length=1 units=m
solve
